400
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,420
Marine Corps scout snipers make their own ghillie suits.

401
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:17,380
They're not allowed to purchase them or buy them anywhere.

402
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:22,160
They have to craft it and construct it from materials that they gather on their own.

403
00:34:22,220 --> 00:34:33,420
Handmade with string netting, stuffed with rags, and topped off with cut branches, the ghillie suit is the only military uniform that is anything but uniform.

404
00:34:36,260 --> 00:34:39,700
But then the ghillie was created by hunters, not soldiers.

405
00:34:40,340 --> 00:34:45,940
The ghillie suit originated from game wardens who worked on the property of 18th century Scottish landlords.

406
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:51,480
Game wardens used these suits to hide themselves from poachers coming onto their landlord's property.

407
00:34:52,220 --> 00:34:59,640
Handcrafted from frayed, dangling rags, the suit's unique ability to break up the human silhouette didn't escape the military.

408
00:35:00,900 --> 00:35:05,700
The ghillie suit was first used by the military in World War I in anti-sniping activity.

409
00:35:10,900 --> 00:35:13,320
Ghillie suits recently returned to their roots.

410
00:35:14,340 --> 00:35:17,920
Hunters by the thousands are buying them for the same reason snipers use them.

411
00:35:18,640 --> 00:35:22,060
To hide from their prey so they can take their best shot.

412
00:35:22,220 --> 00:35:30,260
